  postAuthor: Koffi Adeyemi
  authorImage: {fileID: 0}
  postHeader: 
  postContent: "Contrary to the perpetual \u201Chigh-risk\u201D narrative, African
    exchanges have outperformed several global peers this quarter\u2014yet most analysts
    still warn investors off the continent.\n"
  funFact_Hint: Think about which headlines you usually see about these markets.
  BiasChoices:
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 1
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: It pushes back at a media environment that habitually
      emphasizes risk over reward.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 0
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: That would be about choosing what to cover, not
      the overall negative tone.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 9
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: Spin slants interpretation; here the focus is on
      the general negative outlook.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 6
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: Confirmation bias is selective data-picking; this
      is a broader crisis framing.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 3
